# The build only COPYs pyproject.toml, constraints.txt, README.md and src/, so this file is
# about how much gets shipped to the daemon rather than what lands in the image. A 60MB
# context on every `docker build` is a slow edit-test loop for no benefit.
#
# One entry is a security exclusion rather than a size one: `.env`. It is in nobody's build,
# but a stray `COPY . .` added later would put a credential in an image layer, and layers are
# published.

.env
.env.*

.venv/
.git/
.github/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# Outputs, not inputs. `traces/` is a mount point at run time.
traces/
*.html
*.zip

# Not needed to build or run the tribunal; the image reviews code mounted at /code.
tests/
docs/
examples/
do.txt
